## Phase 1 execution model — SETTLED (Plan B, 2026-08-31)

After extensive testing (chunked-typing, CDP, userscript, image
matching, diff-clicking — all documented in `test.md`), the settled
architecture is **"script opens product pages one by one, you click
save-to-list"**:

1. **Wednesday**: reminder arrives → you copy the 3 WW lists into the
   sheet manually → the script updates the sheet and sends you:
   - **Unmatched** (skip / add / forget)
   - **Wool missing** + **Coles missing** (add / forget)
   - **Price-unavailable list** — items with a sheet price that
     returned "price unavailable" this week; week-count per item;
     every item has a 3-letter code; `delete code aaa,bbb` removes;
     unmentioned items stay tracked; recovered items auto-leave.
2. **"Add"** → price into the sheet + item joins the **to-do list**.
3. **To-do run** (`/run-todo` in Claw): the script opens each item's
   exact product page (stockcode URL, title-verified) one by one —
   no clicking, no scrolling — you add it and reply per item:
   - `/done` → added → consumed from the queue
   - `/skip` → stays in the queue for next run
   - `/wrong` → not the right item → choose:
     - `manual` → moves to the **manual list** (you handle it)
     - `forget` → **permanent forget list** (never appears on any
       list again)
4. **Searched/compare run** (`/run-searched`, mid-week or Wednesday
   morning before the sync): same open-pages loop over the searched
   queue.
5. **Shopping-list automation**: scrapped for now.

## Time to a working Phase 1

- Data layer + Plan B engine: done (open-pages loop, price-unavailable
  tracker, manual/forget lists, chat commands).
- Remaining: Wednesday-pipeline integration (feed unavailable items to
  the tracker after the compare) + first live Wednesday run.

